                { "key": "adminUid", "value": "",    "description": "Filter by admin Firebase UID", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "📌 NO DATA NEEDED.\n\nReturns: { success, count, logs[] }\n\nEach log has:\n- id (Firestore doc ID)\n- action (e.g. CREATE_COURSE)\n- adminUid (who made the call)\n- targetUid (entity created/updated/deleted)\n- timestamp\n- ipAddress\n- details (the request body)\n\n⚠️ Returns count:0 if no actions have been logged yet (run folders 01-08 first).\n\n💡 TIP: You can also see these directly in the Firebase Emulator UI:\nhttp://localhost:4000 → Firestore tab → system_audit_logs collection"
